{
  "version": 8,
  "dashboardId": "business_metrics",
  "title": "Business Metrics",
  "description": "Business signal only: registrations, users by auth type, orders and their delivery state, and email outcomes. HTTP status codes are deliberately NOT here \u2014 they are technical health, not business, and each service's own Golden Signals dashboard already carries them. Two tabs: \"At a glance\" for the current number of each metric, \"Trends\" for how it moved. PANELS USE PromQL, NOT SQL: the UI dispatches on queryType, and a metrics stream queried with queryType sql renders 'Error Loading Data' without ever issuing a search request. Dimension names arrive prefixed and lowercased (CloudWatch `Service` -> `dimensions_service`), and the metric name becomes the stream name (amazonaws.com/3MRAI/orders_total -> amazonaws_com_3mrai_orders_total). Gauges use max(); counters use sum().",
  "role": "",
  "owner": "3MRAI",
  "created": "2026-08-12T00:00:00.000Z",
  "tabs": [
    {
      "tabId": "trends",
